      "content": "That's a solid start, thanks. It feels professional and captures the notes well. \n\nI just ran it through the tool and the \"Richness Score\" came back pretty low—like, the editors are going to think it's a bit thin for a feature piece. They really want that \"vivid, sensory experience\" feel. \n\nCould you try expanding it a bit? I need it to be more evocative and \"lush\" to get a better score on the tool, but I'm still stressing: please don't just pile on descriptors for the sake of it. I don't want it to look like you're just trying to game the adjective count. Just try to make the descriptions deeper and more colorful so it actually feels 'rich' to a reader.",
